#47029
&+cThe &+yBoarding Platform &+cof &+LThe &+cIron&+Lhold &+CG&+crudg&+Ce&N~
   &+cThe deck of &+LThe &+cIron&+Lhold &+CG&+crudg&+Ce&+c is more of a fortress than
&+ca ferry, constantly the stage of nonstop business from its'
&+cdwarven hosts. At both the front and rear, raised platforms
&+chouse massive swivel-mounted ballistae that are manned at all
&+chours. The broad sides are reinforced with iron plating to
&+csupport the weight of heavy catapults. Positioned on both
&+cport and starboard sides, these engines are typically loaded
&+cwith jagged rubble or "fire-pots", ensuring &+LThe &+cIron&+Lhold &+CG&+crudg&+Ce
&+ccan clear a path through blockades or hostile flotillas.
~
