&+y   The deck of the Stalval is a sprawling expanse of grey-
&+yish driftwood and whalebone, bleached by the salt and sun
&+Cof the northern seas. The central length of the Stalval
&+Chas massive ribs of the Great Whale arching upward from the
&+ygunwales to create a skeletal, open-air ribcage over the
&+yrowing benches. Every inch of the timber is etched with
&+Cswirling, tribal carvings depicting the Great Whale's
&+Cbattles against the kraken and other sea behemoths.
&+y   Smoke rises from the center of the vessel, where a massive
&+yfire-pit burns perpetually in a built-in stone fire pit. The
&+Centire deck groans with a deep, rhythmic sound of the ship's
&+Chull stressing against the forces of nature.
~
