#47104
&+yThe &+RH&+Wi&+Rg&+Wh &+RS&+We&+Ra&+Wt &+yof The &+CStalval&N~
&+C   Rising just past the shimmering heat of the firepit to the
&+Weast, the Jarl's Command Platform looms like a jagged throne
&+Wof bone and iron. The structure is constructed from the massive,
&+Cfused vertebrae of a kraken, tiered upward to give the jarl a
&+Wclear view over the rowing benches below, and beyond into the
&+Wchurning horizon. Thick, overlapping mantles of white fur and
&+Csilver-grey seal-hide drape over the railings, providing a
&+Wwindbreak against the biting gales that howl through the aft-
&+Wribs of the vessel. At the center of the platform stands the
&+CJarl's High Seat, a chair carved from a single mammoth skull.
~
