&+Lartery. The air here is a suffocating mixture of fermented shark
&+rmeat, stale sweat, and salty sea air. The ship rises and falls
&+rwith the sea, occasionally jolting as she breaks the wakes ahead
&+Lof her. The ceiling is low, made of crisscrossed iron and wood.
&+LThere are no port-holes to the sea below deck, only bilge bunks
&+Land brig cells.
~
